---------------------------------------------------------------------------
PARITY MAPPING (web → native)
---------------------------------------------------------------------------
  data:   ChartDataPoint slice { time, elevation(m SI), speed } + DriveStats
            { elevGain, elevLoss }                       → ElevationSample
            { index, time, elevationM, speedMps } (SI floor; speed kept in m/s and
            converted only at the display boundary per ADR-004) + ElevationStats.
  speed:  web pre-converts speed via convertSpeedFromSI(mps, unitPrefs.speed)
            ('km/h'=mps*3600/1000, 'mph'=mps*3600/1609.344) → SpeedUnit.convert +
            ElevationProjection.points(from:speedUnit:); the unit label is the bare
            pref string ("Speed (km/h)" / "Speed (mph)").
  stats:  web parent reduction elevGain=Σ max(0,Δ) / elevLoss=Σ max(0,-Δ) over the
            consecutive elevation samples; Net = elevGain - elevLoss
            → ElevationProjection.stats (self-contained + unit-tested).
  shell:  <ChartContainer title="Elevation Profile" height 220> inside <FadeIn>
            → TSFadeIn + tokenized glass card (Color.TS.surface + TSRadius.lg +
            Color.TS.border), header + gain/loss/net stat row + legend.
  chart:  Recharts ComposedChart — <Area dataKey=elevation> (#10b981, fill .2,
            left axis) + <Line dataKey=speed> (#a855f7, opacity .6, right axis),
            CartesianGrid, dual y-axes, synced ReferenceLine → Swift Charts Chart{
            AreaMark(elevation, gradient) + LineMark(elevation stroke, statusSuccess
            width 2) + LineMark(speed, chartSeriesPower .6 width 1.5) }. Swift Charts
            plots ONE y-scale per Chart, so the web's two axes are reproduced REALLY
            (not collapsed): the LEFT scale stays in elevation meters and the speed
            line is projected into that domain (projectSpeedToElevation) while a
            TRAILING AxisMarks reads the true speed back out. X is the sample index
            with start/end time labels (web interval="preserveStartEnd").
  colors: elevation #10b981 → Color.TS.statusSuccess (adaptive); speed #a855f7 →
            Color.TS.chartSeriesPower (purple) at 0.6 opacity (web strokeOpacity .6).
  cursor: useSyncedCursor (broadcast onMouseMove) + useSyncedReferenceLineX (read
            syncedX) → ElevationCursorSync seam (the shared drive-detail cursor):
            .chartXSelection broadcasts the local hover via model.updateCursor; the
            RuleMark + tooltip follow model.cursorIndex, so a sibling chart's hover
            moves this surface's reference line too (bidirectional, tested).
  tip:    <Tooltip content={<ChartTooltip/>}> → ElevationTooltip via the RuleMark
            annotation (time + Elevation X m + Speed Y unit).
  legend: web <Legend> series names "Elevation (m)" / "Speed (unit)"
            → ElevationMetricLegend (solid + faded line swatch).
  empty:  web `chartData.length > 1 ? <chart> : <Activity glyph + "No telemetry
            data available">` → resolvePhase threshold (> 1) + ElevationEmpty
            (ContentUnavailableView, waveform.path.ecg). Never a blank box.
  i18n:   every t(key,default) from source resolved through ElevationStrings facade
            (table "ElevationChart"); series names + units localized (fallbacks
            identical to the web strings) so no English literal ships in code.

STATES (every one renders — no hidden surface):
  loading  → ElevationLoadingChart (TSSkeleton stat row + chart block; reduce-motion)
  content  → ElevationStatRow (gain/loss/net) + ElevationProfileChart + metric legend
  empty    → ElevationEmpty (web "No telemetry data available") — never blank
  error    → ElevationError (QueryError-equiv, Retry → model.refresh())
  stale    → freshness chip (Stale) + connectivity banner + one guarded auto-refresh
  offline  → freshness chip (Offline) + banner; keeps the cached trace, no refetch
a11y: container summary (title + gain/loss/net + max speed), chart aria label +
  spoken summary value, per-sample cursor label, stat-row + legend + chip combined
  labels, reduce-motion animation gate, Dynamic Type via system fonts/tokens. The
  web chart opts out of a per-sample table (its `chart-a11y:no-table` marker); native
  matches that with a concise spoken summary rather than reading every sample.
telemetry: P1/S11 view.opened(surface:"ElevationChart") emitted once on appear.

